WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.430
CRAIG WILEY: Hi,
my name's Craig,

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.910
and I'm the Director of
Product Management for Cloud AI

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.792
Platform here at
Google Platform.

00:00:10.792 --> 00:00:12.750
Today, I'm going to be
talking to you about how

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.890
to create value with the breadth
and depth of our AI platform.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.990
Creating value with
the platform simply

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.650
comes down to putting the best
of Google's AI technologies

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.950
to work for you and
for your company.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.160
What does this mean?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.370
Fundamentally, this
means, how can we

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.490
map your business strategy
to the right AI absorption

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.732
strategy?

00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:36.190
We'll talk about
the different ways

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.070
that Google helps you deploy
AI without compromising

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.660
on flexibility, speed,
quality, or scale.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.850
And finally, we'll
talk about some

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.740
of the customers
that have transformed

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:53.010
their businesses by tapping
into the innovation from Google.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.770
As I think about AI,
fundamentally, AI only

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.400
does two things.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.470
One, it helps you
grow your market,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:02.640
increased subscribership,
increase users,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.450
increase their spend, or
increase their conversion.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.900
Or it helps you in the back
end drive efficiencies,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.420
reduce costs, drive out
waste from the system.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.690
Together, these two
capabilities allow

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:23.510
you to achieve previously
unimaginable results

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:28.270
for you and for your company
using this critical technology

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:33.230
AI is not limited to this
business or that industry.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:35.270
Opportunities to
use AI can be found

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.090
in every vertical,
whether it's retail,

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.390
our capabilities in
health, financial services,

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:45.050
things like lending or
anti-money laundering, media

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.360
and entertainment, or
industrial manufacturing

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.540
with things like visual
inspection capabilities,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.860
or public sector.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.410
All of these are rich
with opportunities.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.960
All of these are areas that
we're helping and work on

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.780
with AI.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.233
As you think about AI
investments and AI absorption,

00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:05.900
when you think about
what Google offers,

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.000
you can really break it
down into three levels

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.389
of investment.

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:12.320
The first is, AI out of the box.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.140
This is very low-investment,
very quick to market,

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.110
but doesn't come with
a lot of customization.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.630
The second is
deploying custom AI.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:23.510
This, on the other hand,
does allow for customization.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.460
It takes a bit more
effort, but it's still

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.140
very quick to market.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.690
And lastly is building
end-to-end AI.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.580
This is when you and the
data scientists you work with

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.300
invest to build your own bespoke
models for areas where this

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.340
will be critical
to your company's

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:46.400
strategic innovation or your
differentiation in the market.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.620
We can think about these three
levels with this example.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.150
The first example of the
AI right out of the box

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.060
would be something like
optical character recognition.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.790
You could imagine simply
calling our Vision API

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.710
to quickly and easily read the
documents that you may have.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.690
Second would be something
like, potentially,

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.580
content classification.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.970
This is an area where "The New
York Times" invested with us

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:15.260
on using AutoML to quickly
and easily classify

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.170
their entire content library.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:22.300
And then finally, we come
to actual, pure insight

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.860
generation, deep investments
that provide unique benefit.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:30.760
This can be seen wonderfully
with Kaggle, an organization

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.070
that we run that
has competitions

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.960
for data scientists
and the work they've

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.350
been doing seeking to
extract critical findings

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.980
from the academic literature
around COVID and SARS viruses.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.780
These three levels
of understanding

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.330
can be seen in our
products as well.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.690
At the first layer, we
see pre-trained APIs.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:57.590
These require no real work from
you to-- all you need to do

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.210
is integrate with the API.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.310
No data science is
needed from you.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.580
Instead, you can simply
get your image labeled,

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:09.590
get your document understood, do
entity extraction or sentiment

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.270
analysis on your document.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:15.050
Or in this case, you can see
using pre-trained Video APIs

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.800
to track movement or track
an object across frames.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.709
Second would be
customer AI with AutoML.

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:25.680
With this capability-- say our
models don't have the objects

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.570
you need labeled.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.660
You want specific fish labeled,
not just "that's a fish",

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.240
but you want to know
what species it is.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.690
You can take your own photos,
quickly and easily label them

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.990
with our data labeling
service, and then move them in

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.350
and train your own AI
model with no code having

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.080
had to been written.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.440
And finally, for those
more powerful models

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.740
or more interesting
and bespoke use cases,

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:56.030
we offer the full end-to-end
capability with our core tools.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.680
You can think of it this way.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.220
Across the top of the stack, we
have our applications, Vision

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:07.110
and Video, Conversation,
Language, and Structured Data.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.930
So whether it's
labeling an image

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:11.450
or working with
video, whether it's

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.120
speech to text, text to
speech, or setting up

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.350
a conversational bot, whether
it's translation, or entity

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.170
extraction, or
sentiment analysis,

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.240
you have all of your needs
with our language capabilities.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.940
And finally, with
Structured Data,

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:28.400
you can build models
on your structured data

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.160
without Python or any
sort of coding required.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.740
Then beneath those
applications we

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.120
have the core tools designed to
help the data scientists build

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.580
the powerful models they want
to both explore and build,

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.900
whether it's notebooks as
a service, data labeling,

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.930
training as a service,
prediction as a service,

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.850
all of the critical
components you'll

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.300
need to ensure that you're
building the best AI.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.180
We're excited to announce
some new capabilities coming.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.520
For example, later
this year, we'll

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.280
have new, improved
workflows for AutoML

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.820
within the console, a
fully integrated experience

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.560
no longer requiring you to make
specific decisions and choices,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.840
but instead making it all
easy right out of the box.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.350
You can see that
with our stack you

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.960
can start by creating
a data set and then

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.420
quickly and easily,
with no code required,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.630
move all the way through to
a model deployment, putting

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.080
your model into production,
ready to be called in a highly

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.060
autoscaling environment.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.600
Now, for those that wish to do
something more sophisticated

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.460
or who wish to build
their own model,

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.730
they'll have the full
capability to do so as well.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:46.020
As we move beyond AutoML, one
primary area investment for us

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:49.140
has been machined
learning ops or MLOps.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.450
In this area, nothing has
been as exciting to us

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:55.500
as what we've seen customers
do with our managed pipelines.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:59.250
Using those managed pipelines
as well as a feature store,

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.520
continuous monitoring of
models that are in production,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.130
and metadata to
help make decisions,

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:09.390
customers will now be able
to support both a fully CI/CD

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:13.530
capability, as well as to
start creating pipelines that

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:17.940
will support much more
sophisticated operations

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.610
such as quickly and easily
retraining your model

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.860
once skew or drift is detected.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.630
These pipelines--
what they do is

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.840
they allow you to take
your monolith of code

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.850
that you've used
to build this model

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.250
and break it down into each
of the individual components.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.933
Now it's much more easily
debugged and understood,

00:07:36.933 --> 00:07:38.350
as well as these
components can be

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.388
saved for future model usage.

00:07:40.388 --> 00:07:42.430
And in the future, when
you are building a model,

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.680
instead of starting
with a blinking cursor,

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.540
you can simply go in
pipelines and start

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.730
pulling in the most
commonly used pipelines

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.970
down into your model
to use for things

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:57.110
like extracting data, validating
data, or evaluating the model.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:08:00.280
These capabilities
significantly reduce

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:02.330
the time of experimentation.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.420
We had one customer
telling us that they

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.880
have increased their
rate of experimentation

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.420
by 7x using this technology.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.820
We couldn't be
more excited to see

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:15.280
how your company will use this.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.970
Finally, as is critical to
any service of this type,

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.970
metadata management
is a key piece

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:25.670
of what we believe is
needed to effectively run

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.790
a MLOps environment.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:31.080
Whether that's the automatic
metadata logging from our

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.059
posted services or
custom metrics that you

00:08:34.059 --> 00:08:38.470
may want to device, both are
quickly and easily captured

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.950
and then can be used for
things like compliance, MLOps,

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.590
continuous training and
continuous delivery,

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:49.070
or experimentation development,
model and artifact comparisons,

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.940
as well as improved
ML reproducibility

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.730
and explainability.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.540
The compliance story here
is an interesting one.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.590
It allows you to do previously
very difficult tasks,

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.320
things like-- imagine if a
customer said, hey, please

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.900
remove me from your records.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.880
All you would have to do
is remove the customer

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.850
from the data set in
question or from all

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.770
of the data sets
that they're in,

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:15.310
and then with pipelines
and ML Metadata,

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:17.830
you could very quickly
and easily auto retrain

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.980
just by determining the fact
that the data set had been

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.560
changed, automatically
retrain the model

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:26.200
and redeploy the model
without a human ever

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.730
having to write code to do so.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.920
We're proud of our AI Platform
because our AI Platform

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.080
does three things really well.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.280
One, it meets our
users where they are.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:42.920
Two, it quickly deploys the
highest quality AI, and three,

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.440
it allows you to
scale and streamline

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:49.595
not a AI in unbelievable ways.

00:09:49.595 --> 00:09:50.970
Meeting customers
where they are?

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.270
What does that mean?

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.450
Well, as you can see
here, I think we all

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.540
fall somewhere on the spectrum
of skills and capabilities

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.850
within machine learning,
and whether you're

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.160
someone who's just starting
out or whether you're

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.260
someone who is already
comfortable with the most

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.830
sophisticated tooling, we
have solutions for you.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.565
When we talk about meeting
customers where they are,

00:10:11.565 --> 00:10:14.570
there's two companies that
are interesting to call out.

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:15.970
The first is cruise.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.520
Cruise is an autonomous
vehicle company

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:20.740
making tremendous
strides in moving

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:22.630
to a world where my
son will never have

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:24.910
to get his driver's license.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:28.510
With this, Cruise builds models,
and we have worked closely

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:30.790
with them on optimizing
their environments

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.090
and optimizing their TensorFlow
capabilities to decrease

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:37.540
their training times so that
they can more quickly and more

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:41.410
easily cycle through
experiments and move

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.740
towards a world in which
cars are fully autonomous.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.890
Now, on the other side
is the city of Memphis.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.870
The city of Memphis is
not traditionally known

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.880
as a tremendous machine learning
powerhouse, but in this case,

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.810
they were actually building
a model very similar to ones

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:57.910
that Cruise has, no
doubt, had to build.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.310
The city of Memphis
wanted to understand

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:03.430
where they had in the
most problematic potholes,

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:07.570
so they used AutoML to
build a pothole detector

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:10.840
and, sure enough, we're
able to save $20,000 a year

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:12.970
in the reduction
in claims costs due

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.400
to these unaddressed potholes.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.260
As you can imagine,
these two customers

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.870
come with very different
skills and expertise,

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.330
and both were able to find
tremendous value with Google

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.040
and its Platform.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:27.320
We do seek, as I said, to
meet customers where they are.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.100
So for example, our AI
Notebooks-- not only

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.800
